        "original_id": "3edf0acb-98dd-54ad-92b1-cad60ab0fd6e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jean Claude Trichet, Mario Draghi, Silvio Berlusconi\n- Organizations: European Central Bank, Financial Stability Board, Bank of Italy, Italian government\n- Events: European banks crisis, ECB letter to Italy on 5 August 2011\n- Roles: ECB President, Financial Stability Board Chairman, Bank of Italy Governor\n\nFacts:\n- Mario Draghi was born on 3 September 1947 and is an Italian economist.\n- Mario Draghi served as Governor of the Bank of Italy from 2005 to 2011.\n- Mario Draghi served as Chairman of the Financial Stability Board from 2009 to 2011.\n- On 5 August 2011, during the European banks crisis, Jean Claude Trichet and Mario Draghi wrote a secret letter to the Italian government led by Silvio Berlusconi.\n- The 5 August 2011 ECB letter urged the Italian government to adopt a series of economic measures as soon as possible.\n- Mario Draghi has served as President of the European Central Bank since November 2011.",
